WEBVTT

00:00:01.330 --> 00:00:05.521
The throughput claim is in config.json, not the blog.

00:00:05.521 --> 00:00:09.712
A 1B maths model with no tokens-per-second figure published.

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:16.736
The pitch, from Paradigma's release blog: High-throughput solutions of difficult mathematical problems.

00:00:17.800 --> 00:00:20.115
Attention blocks in config.json.

00:00:20.115 --> 00:00:24.746
36 of 48: run a 1,024-token sliding window.

00:00:24.746 --> 00:00:28.219
The other 12 run global attention.

00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:32.667
KV cache at 131,072 tokens.

00:00:32.667 --> 00:00:39.401
All 48 blocks global, 6.44 GB; as configured, 1.65 GB.

00:00:39.401 --> 00:00:42.768
Arithmetic on four config fields.

00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:47.833
A concurrency claim, not a speed claim, and the ceiling, not a measurement.

00:00:49.250 --> 00:00:55.108
Every number here is from the full article, with its sources, at ai.thesatyajit.com.
